    name="6 Dissemination and Service Delivery Value Stream"
    id="id-b593b45525374db5a5c75ac34775a14e"
    documentation="Purpose:&#xD;&#xA;To provide users with secure, accessible, and user-centric access to statistical outputs, ensuring transparency, usability, and impact.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Description:&#xD;&#xA;This value stream delivers the final stage of value creation — transforming internal statistical products into externally consumable services. It includes data publication, visualization, reporting, and the operation of access services such as open data portals, research environments, and APIs.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Value is created through trust, transparency, and impact: ensuring users can find, access, and understand official statistics and research data.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The main artefacts are published datasets, statistical releases, and data access services. This stage completes the statistical value chain, fulfilling the organization’s mission of providing objective, high-quality information for decision-making and research.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Key capabilities: Data Dissemination, Access Control, User Support &amp; Service Management, Metadata Publication, Communication &amp; Outreach."
    viewpoint="value_stream">
